{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791223597,"nonce":"GaUNgcJ/pXIINxfAX05zzerj5N4=","message":"Root cause: with the embedded stdlib snapshot, a merged module's external_function_names can hold a stale record that shares its id with one of the module's own extern declarations (here StringTools.trim on the id of EReg's haxe_register_interface_impl). fixup_stale_cross_module_refs (crossmodule.rs, run again by finalize_mir_references in the runner, AOT and preblade) trusted the name record first and rebound the 2-arg registration call in EReg's __vtable_init__ to a 1-arg StringTools function (crash in rtrim). rayzor run never calls finalize, which is why the CLI worked. Reproduced on the nuc only with a snapshot whose compiler id matches (snapshot-gen, then touch compiler/build.rs, then build); without one the stdlib is lowered from source and the record never collides. Fix: a name record no longer rewrites a call whose own id the module declares when the named target's parameter count differs from the call's argument count. regexredux now runs on cranelift/llvm/tiered with the snapshot (21-24 ms on the nuc).","files":null}]}